  id: Scene08_FAQ_3
  speaker: WATTSON
  text: We could, but Ohm's torsion galvanometer needed a steady hand and a lot of
    patience, and his thermoelectric source gave only a tiny push. Today's ammeter
    and voltmeter give clear numbers straight away, so we can see the relationship
    much more clearly.
